@startuml note-update-sequence
' Author: Carlos Scheidecker
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
hide footbox
title RestNotes - conditional note update and atomic snapshot
footer Author: Carlos Scheidecker
autonumber

actor Client
boundary NoteController as Api
control NoteService as Service
control "LockedNotes\nNoteWriteAccess" as Access
control NoteLocks as Guard
participant "NoteLockStore\nJDBC" as Store
participant "JPA repositories /\nEntityManager" as Jpa
database MySQL as Db

note over Client,Api
  Bearer authentication and DTO/body validation occur first.
  Existing-note PUT/PATCH and tag writes share this guard.
end note
Client -> Api : PATCH /notes/{id}\nIf-Match + optional Note-Lock-Token
Api -> Service : patch(note, actor, condition, DTO, token)
group Spring write transaction - READ_COMMITTED / timeout 15s
  Service -> Access : require authorized current note
  Access -> Jpa : scalar scope / candidate access paths
  Jpa -> Db : scoped lookups (avoid stale managed entity)
  Access -> Jpa : lock sorted owner/access-path teams\nthen notebook; refresh capabilities
  Jpa -> Db : current locking reads
  Access -> Jpa : lock + refresh note
  Jpa -> Db : SELECT FOR UPDATE
  Access -> Access : require EDITOR-or-higher\ncheck archive and caller-scoped note ETag
  alt inaccessible / insufficient role / invalid condition
    Access --> Service : 404 / 403 / 428 / 400 / 412\nor 409 ACCESS_CHANGED
    Service -> Db : rollback / release locks
    Service --> Api : static Problem Details
    Api --> Client : failed request; no mutation
  else authorized and current
    Access --> Service : locked note + notebook capability
    Service -> Guard : requireWrite(note, actor, token)
    Guard -> Guard : validate token format\nreject malformed input before lease query
    Guard -> Store : now() and find(noteId)
    Store -> Db : database UTC time AFTER locks\nread lease metadata / digest
    Db --> Store : deadline / owner / verifier
    Store --> Guard : lease or absent
    Guard -> Guard : check expiry / owner\nconstant-time digest comparison
    alt missing active-holder credential / stale token
      Guard --> Service : 423 / 409 (malformed token: 400)
      Service -> Db : rollback / release locks
      Service --> Api : static Problem Details
      Api --> Client : no content/history/activity change
    else write permitted
      Guard --> Service : allowed (unlocked or valid holder)
      Service -> Service : validate patch semantics / content bytes
      alt unchanged representation
        Service -> Db : commit without aggregate changes
        Service --> Api : unchanged NoteResponse / ETag
      else real content or pinning change
        Service -> Jpa : apply changes / flush note version
        Jpa -> Db : UPDATE notes
        Service -> Jpa : latest history version + 1\nsave immutable snapshot with sorted tags
        Jpa -> Db : INSERT note_history
        Service -> Jpa : save NOTE_UPDATED activity
        Jpa -> Db : INSERT activity_logs (flush by commit)
        Service -> Db : commit ALL changes / release locks
        Service --> Api : NoteResponse / updated ETag
      end
      Api --> Client : 200 after successful transaction commit
    end
  end
end
note over Service,Db
  Any validation/persistence/commit failure rolls back the whole transaction.
  JPA row version and history sequence are independent.
  Archive records activity without a duplicate snapshot and removes its lease.
end note
@enduml
